# 126 · UI clean-up: every screen checked against the rules for screens, and the gaps fixed

**Status:** `PROPOSED` · **Version:** [v0.2.0](../roadmap.md#v020)

## What

A plan only; nothing of it is done.

The dashboard grew one screen at a time. This goal checks every screen against the rules for screens, records each gap here, and fixes them:

- every form label has a description in its ⓘ;
- cards, call-outs and summaries use plain words (Simplified Technical English);
- each action says what it decides and what happens next, before and after the click;
- each button shows at once that it was pressed, and shows its outcome without a refresh;
- the same thing has the same name, the same word and the same look on every screen.

The other goals of v0.1.4 improve one screen each. This one makes the screens agree with each other.

## Why

The owner, 2026-10-24: "v0.1.4 becomes UI Cleanup and UX improvements."

## Constraints

- **A mockup first** ([rules for every goal](../README.md#rules-for-every-goal)): a real change to a screen is mocked up and shown to the owner before it is built.
- **Docs follow the code:** each fix updates the pages that describe the screen, its words and its screenshots, in the same commit.

## Done when

- [ ] Every screen is checked, and its gaps are recorded here.
- [ ] Each gap is fixed, after the owner approved its mockup, or has a recorded reason to stay.
- [ ] The pages and the screenshots match the screens.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-24, owner: v0.1.4 is the UI clean-up and UX improvements.

## Open questions

- Whether this check and goal [089](089-dashboard-performance.goal)'s faster pages go through the screens together.

## Progress

- 2026-10-24: Goal written from the owner's words.

